97. Notes with concern that public procurement weaknesses remain the largest source of irregular payments; highlights that the Court made 38 observations on public procurement weaknesses in 2023 (compared to 41 in 2022 and 28 in 2021)27 ; urges agencies to introduce measures to ensure strict adherence to procurement regulations and the principles of transparency, competition and cost-effectiveness; reminds the need for regular training programs for staff on financial management, procurement rules and fraud prevention; calls for stricter accountability measures ensuring that any persistent deficiencies lead to targeted corrective actions and consequences for repeated non-compliance; notes that the recurrent non-compliance with public procurement rules highlights a certain amateurism of the agencies concerned and damages their image, their credibility but also the image of the Union in addition to legally exposing the agencies concerned;

---

27 ECA report, p. 37. Only observations that refer to the agencies part of this resolution.
